  example:{title:"one procedure, one external tool, one policy hook",intro:"Build a release workflow whose instructions, service access, and deterministic guard remain separate.",steps:["Write a release-review skill.","Configure a project-scoped read-only tracker MCP endpoint using environment references.","Run MCP doctor and authenticate outside committed config.","Add a <code>PreToolUse</code> shell matcher.","Explicitly deny pushes to the protected branch.","Inspect discovery and trust state.","Invoke the skill and discover the MCP read tool.","Verify a prohibited push is blocked even when requested."],code:"grok mcp add --transport http --scope project tracker https://mcp.example.com/mcp\ngrok mcp doctor tracker\ngrok inspect",lang:"bash",interpretation:"The endpoint is illustrative; the command shapes are documented. Actual tools and authentication depend on the service.",verify:"Record skill origin, qualified MCP name, trust state, hook decision JSON, and unchanged protected branch."},
